{
  "Levit.14.21.17-c.html": "<HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[26 Jul 2022]: \n     Changes file: 2022.07.04 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.04.03, number: 10 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Leviticus 14:21.17</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Leviticus 14:21.17</h1>\n  <h2>Move merkha to bet; add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.07.04 - Changes/images/2022.04.03/10-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>A merkha can not be on the bet for vocalization; it belongs on the lamed. The mark in the LC is ill-positioned.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b>2022.07.04 - Changes.xml : 2022.04.03-10\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Levit.25.20.4-c.html": "<html>\n<header profile=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/11/profile\" > \n        <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/> \n        <title>Leviticus 25:20.4</title>\n</header>\n    \n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n        <h1>Leviticus 25:20.4</h1>\n        <h4>The UXLC transcribes the LC by placing two accents (mahapakh, tipeha) on the kaf.</h4>\n        <table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5pt\"><tr><td>\n            <center>\n                <img src=\"../../Changes/2021.04.01 - Changes/images/2020.12.22/2-Detail.jpg\" border=\"4pt\"/>\n            </center>\n        </td></tr>\n        <p/>\n        <tr><td>\n            <center><i>Credit: Photograph by Bruce and Kenneth Zuckerman, West Semitic Research, \n            in collaboration with Ancient Biblical Manuscript Center. \n            Courtesy National Library of Russia (Saltykov-Shchedrin). \n            </i></center>\n        </td></tr>\n        </table>\n        <p/>\n        Two markings on this word are a peculiarity of the Leningrad Codex. \n        <p/>\n        <ul>\n        <li>The mahapakh doesn't make sense as an alternative to the tipeha.</li>\n        <p/>\n        <li>There is no tradition of what a combined mahapakh-tipeha would mean.</li>\n        <p/>\n        <li>There is no tradition of a specialized presentation of alternatives \n          as in the Decalogues/Reuven Saga.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <p/>\n        The \"Miqra according to the Masorah\" doesn't have the mahapakh on the kaf.\n        </p>\n        <p/>\n        <table cellpadding=\"10pt\" border=\"1pt\" align=\"center\"><tr><td>\n        Ben Denckla offers this hypothesis:\n        The mahapakh (&#x05e1;&#x05a4) might also be interpreted \n            as a malformed or damaged masorah circle (&#x05e1;&#x05af; )\n               over the word נִזְרָ֔ע below it in the manuscript as shown below.\n        The noted word, Lev  25:20.4 is shown in blue; the word with the \n        putative masorah circle, Lev 25:20.9, is shown in red.     \n        <p/>      \n        <table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5pt\"><tr><td>\n            <center>\n                <img src=\"Leviticus.25.20 - Ben Denckla.png\" border=\"4pt\"/>\n            </center>\n        </td></tr>\n        <tr><td><center><i>\n         Credit: Ben Denckla: 3 March 2021  cropped by cvk to show two lines.\n        </i></center></td></tr>\n        </table>\n        <p/>\n             \n        The interpretation of this mark as an incomplete masorah circle eliminates two problems: \n        <ul>\n          <li>It eliminates the need to explain why a mahapakh would be here. </li>\n           <p/>\n          <li>It also eliminates the need to explain why the line below has two masorah parva notes (ל̇ל̇) \n              but only one masorah circle.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <p/>\n        Masorah circles are typically interrupted at one or two points, as seen in the image.\n        </td></tr><table>\n\n        <p/>\n        <b><i>Ben Denckla</i></b>\n        <p align=\"right\"><b>2021.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2020.12.22-2</b></p>\n        <p/>\n        <table border=\"1pt\" align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"16pt\">\n            <tr><td>\n              <span style=\"color:blue;font-size:14pt\">\n                  <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC\" ('c') notes</a>\n              </span>\n              <p/>\n              <span style=\"color:blue;font-size:14pt\">\n                  <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n              </span>\n            </td?</tr>\n        </table>\n        <p/>\n        </body>\n</html>\n",
  "Levit.26.34.8-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2021.12.28, number: 1 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Leviticus 26:34.8</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Leviticus 26:34.8</h1>\n  <h2>Unexpected hataf qamats on initial he, missing dagesh on shin; add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes/images/2021.12.28/1-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                   The LC has a hataf qamats on the initial he and the following shin lacks a dagesh.\n                   The usual marking has a qamatz on the he and a dagesh on the shin as\n                   in the Miqra according to the Masorah (MAM).\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                   The UXLC transcribes the LC correctly, however.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Todd Shandelman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes.xml?2021.12.28-1\">2022.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2021.12.28-1</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Levit.26.35.3-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2021.12.28, number: 2 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Leviticus 26:35.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Leviticus 26:35.3</h1>\n  <h2>Missing dagesh on shin; add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes/images/2021.12.28/2-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                   The LC has no dagesh on the shin.\n                   The usual marking has a dagesh on the shin as\n                   in the Miqra according to the Masorah (MAM).\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                   The UXLC transcribes the LC correctly, however.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Todd Shandelman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes.xml?2021.12.28-2\">2022.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2021.12.28-2</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Levit.6.3.12-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.05.27, number: 1 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Leviticus 6:3.12</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Leviticus 6:3.12</h1>\n  <h2>Remove segol from sin, add 'c' note. (#2)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.05.27/1-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Ben Denckla</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.05.27-1\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.05.27-1</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Levit.8.11.3-t.html": "<HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[26 Jul 2022]: \n     Changes file: 2022.07.04 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.04.03, number: 4 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Leviticus 8:11.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Leviticus 8:11.3</h1>\n  <h2>Add meteg after patah on ayin; add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.07.04 - Changes/images/2022.04.03/4-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The meteg is light, but well shaped.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b>2022.07.04 - Changes.xml : 2022.04.03-4\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Levit.8.24.5-t.html": "<HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[26 Jul 2022]: \n     Changes file: 2022.07.04 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.04.03, number: 6 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Leviticus 8:24.5</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Leviticus 8:24.5</h1>\n  <h2>Remove dagesh from both yod and tav; add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.07.04 - Changes/images/2022.04.03/6-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>No dagesh at all on the yod. There is a possible, very faint dagesh on the tav.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b>2022.07.04 - Changes.xml : 2022.04.03-6\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Levit.8.28.1-t.html": "<HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[26 Jul 2022]: \n     Changes file: 2022.07.04 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.04.03, number: 7 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Leviticus 8:28.1</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Leviticus 8:28.1</h1>\n  <h2>Remove dagesh on yod; add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.07.04 - Changes/images/2022.04.03/7-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>A possible dagesh on the yod is very faint.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b>2022.07.04 - Changes.xml : 2022.04.03-7\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>"
}
